    "case_id": "721",
    "case_summary": "A 53-year-old female with a medical history significant for being on maintenance therapy with Rituximab every 8 weeks until January 2022. The patient had received two doses of viral vector vaccine (AstraZeneca), with the second dose administered in June 2021.\n\nInitial presentation (March 10th, 2022):- Temperature: 38.2°C- Blood pressure: 122/78 mm Hg- Heart rate: 86 bpm- Oxygen saturation: 96% on room air- Lungs: Clear fields on auscultation- Heart: No abnormal cardiac murmurs\n\nLaboratory Tests:- CRP: 14 mg/L (mildly elevated)- White blood cell count: 6.2 × 10^9/L- Absolute lymphocyte count: 1.42 × 10^9/L (23% of total white blood cells)Imaging Studies:1. Initial Chest CT (March 10th, 2022)- Description: Ground glass opacities and 'crazy paving' pattern bilaterally in the lower lobes2. First Chest X-ray (April 2nd, 2022)- Description: Haziness in both lower lung fields with infiltrations in around 10% of both lungs, consistent with atypical viral pneumonia3. Second Chest X-ray (April 26th, 2022)- Description: Bilateral ground-glass appearance with progression in haziness in both lower and middle lung fields4. Follow-up Chest X-ray (May 14th, 2022)- Description: Improvement in bilateral infiltrationsOther Tests:- RT-PCR test of sputum: Positive for SARS-CoV-2- COVID-19 antibody test: Initially negative (remained negative for approximately 40 days after first positive PCR)",
